{
  "_doc": "The season registry (docs/design/brand/seasons/README.md 'How to add a season'). ONE source, copied byte-for-byte to apps/ios/Wordocious/Resources/season-registry.json and apps/android/app/src/main/assets/season-registry.json (apps/web/lib/season-registry.test.ts checks the copies). Windows live in core SEASON_WINDOWS (\u00d73 ports, level-season-fixtures.json) and must list the same ids. Slots name shipped art (web /art/<name>.webp, iOS image set <name>, Android drawable <name with _>); 'titles' and 'walls' map the NORMAL art name to the seasonal one ('*' = prefix); a light-mode wall twin '<name>-light' wins in light mode. 'castSize' + 'castTrim' = the skins' square size and alpha boxes [x0, y0, x1, y1] (alpha > 8), so the cast row frames any season's skins. Any missing slot or unshipped file falls back to the normal art. 'surfaces' (optional) recolors the app's windows during the season: tone ('dark' = light on-card + on-wall text, dark system chrome / status bar), card + cardOpacity (page cards, game board panel), hero + heroOpacity (the Home hero card), raised (chips inside cards), cap (the game cards' drip trim stops, top -> base; capTint mixes each game's own color into the middle stop), glow (the cards' soft lift color), text / textMuted / textSecondary (on-card ink), headline (the hero greeting lettering: top, bottom, deep, nameTop, nameBottom), bannerGlow (a soft glow behind the hero's banner art) and cobweb (the hero's top-corner web ink; absent = none). The DEBUG key debug-season-surfaces = 'off' (web ?surfaces=off) turns the surfaces off for an A/B (perf, contrast) while the season art stays. Any missing surface slot keeps the normal look.",
